// OTD-0015 - Rogue engineering workstation to PLC
// Library: OT Threat Content  |  Legacy ID: OT-UC-0015
// ATT&CK for ICS: T0859  |  Severity: High
// Detection logic: Detects a designated RDP/jump-server host appearing as a Modbus, DNP3, S7comm, or OPC UA protocol client itself rather than simply brokering an interactive remote session, which can indicate an attacker has installed tooling directly on the jump host to issue OT commands.
//
// STATUS: SCAFFOLD. This detection is catalogued as a specification; the logic below
// expresses the intent against the mapped table but MUST be completed and validated
// against real telemetry before deployment. Placeholders in <angle brackets> are
// environment-specific.
//
OTNetwork_CL
| where TimeGenerated > ago(24h)
// TODO: express the detection condition -- Detects a designated RDP/jump-server host appearing as a Modbus, DNP3, S7comm, or OPC UA protocol client itself rather than simply brokering an interactive remote session, which can indicate an attacker has installed tooling directly on the jump host to issue OT commands.
| where isnotempty(SourceIP)
| summarize Count = count(), FirstSeen = min(TimeGenerated), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated)
    by SourceIP, DestinationIP
| where Count > <THRESHOLD>
| order by Count desc
